'''Sakate Shrine''' (坂手神社) is a Shinto shrine in {{ill|Aichi Prefecture|de|Präfektur Aichi|ja|愛知県|zh|愛知縣}}'s city of {{ill|Ichinomiya|de|Ichinomiya|ja|一宮市|zh|一宮市}}. It was formerly designated as a prefectural shrine under the old shrine ranking system.

The shrine appears in the {{ill|Engi-shiki|de|Engi-shiki|ja|延喜式神名帳|zh|延喜式神名帳}} as the Shikinaisha "Sakate Shrine" of Nakashima District, {{ill|Owari Province|de|Provinz Owari|ja|尾張国|zh|尾張國}} (another theory identifies {{ill|Hiyoshi Shrine|de|Hiyoshi-Schrein|ja|日吉社|zh|日吉社}} in {{ill|Inazawa|de|Inazawa|ja|稲沢市|zh|稻澤市}}). Although the shrine is located in {{ill|Haguri District|de|Haguri-Distrikt|ja|葉栗郡|zh|葉栗郡}} of Owari Province, it is believed to have been part of Nakashima District before the medieval period. The place name {{ill|Sachihara|de|Sachihara|ja|佐千原|zh|佐千原}} is said to have evolved from Sakate → Satehara → Sachihara.

Until the Meiji era, the shrine received sacred textiles from the {{ill|Ise Grand Shrine|de|Ise-Schrein|ja|伊勢神宮|zh|伊勢神宮}} annually. One theory holds that it once served as an administrative office (御厨) of Ise Grand Shrine. It is also said to have been the "Moto Ise" Nakashima-no-miya of Owari Province (another tradition identifies {{ill|Sakami Shrine|de|Sakami-Schrein|ja|酒見神社|zh|酒見神社}}).

== Overview ==

* The date of foundation is unknown. In the 14th year of {{ill|Emperor Suinin|de|Kaiser Suinin|ja|垂仁天皇|zh|垂仁天皇}}, {{ill|Yamato-hime-no-mikoto|de|Yamato-hime-no-mikoto|ja|倭姫命|zh|倭姬命}}—while searching for a site to enshrine the spirit of {{ill|Amaterasu-Ōmikami|de|Amaterasu-Ōmikami|ja|天照大神|zh|天照大神}}—traveled from Ikurakawa-no-miya (present-day {{ill|Tenjin Shrine|de|Tenjin-Schrein|ja|天神神社|zh|天神神社}}, Mizuho) to Nakashima District in Owari Province. It is said she first enshrined the Sakate deity here and placed Amaterasu’s spirit in a temporary shrine just north of the present site.
* During the Edo period it was known as {{ill|Hakken-sha|de|Hakken-sha|ja|八剣社|zh|八剣社}}, but in 1872 (Meiji 5) it was designated a village shrine and in 1941 (Shōwa 16) promoted to a prefectural shrine.

== Deity ==

* {{ill|Takamizukami|de|Takamizukami|ja|高水上神|zh|高水上神}}
* Considered a son of {{ill|Ōyamatsumi|de|Ōyamatsumi|ja|大山祗神|zh|大山祗神}}.

== Access ==

* Take the {{ill|Meitetsu Bus|de|Meitetsu-Bus|ja|名鉄バス|zh|名鐵巴士}} to the "Sachihara" stop (15 min walk) or the "Higashi-Sachihara" stop (10 min walk).
** From {{ill|Meitetsu Ichinomiya Station|de|Meitetsu-Ichinomiya-Bahnhof|ja|名鉄一宮駅|zh|名鐵一宮站}} (platform 3, bus terminal) on the {{ill|Meitetsu Nagoya Main Line|de|Meitetsu-Nagoya-Hauptlinie|ja|名鉄名古屋本線|zh|名鐵名古屋本線}} & Bisai Line and {{ill|JR Owari-Ichinomiya Station|de|JR Owari-Ichinomiya-Bahnhof|ja|尾張一宮駅|zh|尾張一宮站}}.
** Buses bound for "Miyata-hongo" stop at Sachihara; those bound for "Kawashima" stop at Higashi-Sachihara.

